  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Dictionary of Basic Japanese Grammar p. 310",
      "html": "Dictionary of Basic Japanese Grammar p. 310",
      "credits_raw": "anon",
      "content_sha256": "ef89e461e715649ae15112d44f56004ef0ab1daf5801aa92305fe62c11d045bc",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "The Japanese is not natural from the context. It should be 毎年9月の最終日曜日.\nFor example, if the Sunday was 26th, we don't say 9月末（９がつすえ）。\nちなみに、月末（げつまつ） is at the end of month. 下旬（げじゅん） is end of month.",
      "html": "The Japanese is not natural from the context. It should be 毎年9月の最終日曜日.<br/>For example, if the Sunday was 26th, we don't say 9月末（９がつすえ）。<br/>ちなみに、月末（げつまつ） is at the end of month. 下旬（げじゅん） is end of month.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "aeef31449f8dd2386935635154508c96d81e4a98aee165253e1d7e6806e3b476",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "9月末 is read ９がつまつ.\nhmm but I found some sites 毎年○月末の▲曜日…。",
      "html": "9月末 is read ９がつまつ.<br/>hmm but I found some sites 毎年○月末の▲曜日…。",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "a7045035e0cc28c5022b2c6728c2bd53558edfbf4c267de70b892fa9e9c11810",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I agree with Miki. It sounds more natural. If you don't like 最終日曜日、you can say 最後の日曜日.",
      "html": "I agree with Miki. It sounds more natural. If you don't like 最終日曜日、you can say 最後の日曜日.",
      "credits_raw": "bamboo4",
      "content_sha256": "e25ab344fbd7a576d7241e9d36b55d37b1d6e0f4347e8db8a6c8af0816fc7226",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    }
